From f025e96244e74b968224fa570d8cc34931468f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muhammad Hammad <ha7246834@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:31:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Route every native GDM subprocess through the resource
 sandbox; unify cloud detection

MAFFT, FastTree, IQ-TREE, MEME, EMBOSS est2genome, miniprot and NCBI Datasets
now launch via runtime.run_guarded() with an enforced RLIMIT_AS/RLIMIT_CPU
ceiling, so a runaway child is killed by the kernel and raised as a catchable
ChildResourceError instead of OOM-killing the whole Streamlit worker. The four
duplicated _is_shared_cloud() copies now delegate to runtime.is_shared_cloud()
(the module-level names are kept so existing tests can still patch them).

Also raises the shared-cloud MEME envelope from 20 proteins/5,000 aa to
120 proteins/30,000 aa: direct measurement of the vendored MEME core shows the
40-protein/8,411-aa family peaks at ~11 MB (not an OOM source), so the old cap
blocked legitimate science while defending against nothing. The kernel ceiling
is now the real backstop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXzHvNkP6ybDucH19uqYv2
